&nbsp;

So far he story is planned in five stages

&nbsp;

1. <b><u>The beginning of the end!</u></b> Heroes gather and help stop a sect of the cult of Gloom from sacrificing what appears to be a young women to summon an eldritch abomination OR stop what seems to be a new hero in town who has snapped (actually a flesh child) from leveling an old abandoned church (chapter of the Cult of Gloom). They can do ONE of these but both lead to the revelation of the impending conflict of the two groups, gloomweaver and his cult versus Biomancer and his Flesh Children, that is to overtake Angel City.

&nbsp;

2. <u style="font-weight: bold;">Trapped!</u>&nbsp;The party finds that the Cult of Gloom in an attempt to keep the elusive Biomancer in the city they have constructed a magical barrier to keep all of Angel City trapped and the rest of the world out. The party will then have a few encounters between the villains struggles and saving people from mass panic and the accidents it causes. Eventually they will be lead to one of a few different places to remove the barrier (labs, places of magic, that mad scientist hobo with the trashcannon)

&nbsp;

3. <u style="font-weight: bold;">The War of the flesh</u>&nbsp;after prepping their method of barrier breaking they see a massive green tower of flames erupt into the sky and suddenly the dead start walking amongst us once more. Angel City at this point now begins to resemble Raccoon City and the few other heroes of the city are now either dead, dying, zombified, or busy helping the rest of the world. So now it&#39;s a gauntlet to find the bases of the cult or Biomancer and take them out.

&nbsp;

4. <b><u>The Fall</u></b>&nbsp;So the party will fail by either gloomweaver being too powerful or Biomancer being another flesh child and now through some investigations and some NPC assistance they discover a dark figure at the beginning of all of this. The Arcanist, a flesh child who gained sentience and and infiltrated the Cult of Gloom to gain the dark powers needed to exist beyond Biomancer&#39;s plans. They also discover his ability to undo the barrier.

&nbsp;

5. <b style="text-decoration: underline;">The Final Days</b>&nbsp;So the party will discover the lair of the Arcanist and engage into the final fight, while also dealing with sieges from some doppelgänger fleshchildren and some lesser demons summoned by Gloomweaver. The rest is still kinda up in the air.

&nbsp;

&nbsp;
